		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=326#p326"><![CDATA[
Most physics engines have several parameters so the velocity of a bouncing ball becomes zero after a while.<br><br>- Restitution coefficient: less then 100% restitution will bring back the linear velocity after every collision.<br>- velocity damping will generally reduce velocity every timestep<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue Sep 13, 2005 7:00 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
